Z||000010||frontal lobe||04-15-2000||12:43 AM||||Good one, Cooter.  How about a Geo Storm?  Is there a conversion kit to drop a lawn mower engine into it to up the h.p.?<P>Seriously, Toyotas are very reliable so I would go with a '91 mr2 turbo.  300zx twin turbo is going to still be a LOT of money.||||reg||1
Z||000011||turbo86se||04-15-2000||11:33 AM||||I feel for you 87GT, but hang in there. The dealer the absolute last place I go for anything except to show the Fiero off. Isn't there anyone in or near your area to work on Fieros? Seems everywhere I go I find someone. <P>Last summer a local used car dealership had a red 94 300Z with T-Tops, chrome wheels, auto trans (a must in Myrtle Beach summer traffic <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).  It had low miles, so I decided to stop in and take it for a drive. Yeah I considered buying it, but not to replace my forever Fiero obsession. I was so unimpressed with the car, I returned it in less than 20 minutes. My turbo 86SE would run circles around it! It didn't handle very well either. My mechanic looked it over, he said don't ever bring this thing to me when anything goes! <BR>My insurance was going to triple! No thanks! <BR>Before I got my Fiero, I looked at a Nissan Pulsar, cool little car, but gawd-awfully sloow! <BR>My advice is, to hang in there! From your past posts it sounds like a sweet car! I regret selling my 85 coupe three years ago, you'll regret selling the GT! ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cooter||04-15-2000||05:03 PM||||Sniff Sniff... But my other car is a Honda Civic!||||reg||1
Z||000013||iplayazi||04-15-2000||06:27 PM||||What were your problems with gm.. I live in Calgary Alberta so I think we talk the same language.. I had a buddy that HAD a 300 zx.. the repair bills on them can be quite costly, even though I love the look of 300's.. very sweet ride. Kinda like a fiero.. just bigger.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Spyder||04-15-2000||07:41 PM||||I have a pearl white Z,  love it.<BR>The repair bills are crazy and the parts cost out the arse.<BR>If you get one, buy the twin turbo. Trust me.<BR>Here is a link to some great guys that talk 1990+  Zs: (not a better group as us) <A HREF="http://www.twinturbo.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.twinturbo.net/</A> <BR>Check out the frequently asked questions.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Oreif||04-15-2000||10:00 PM||||Geo Storm? NOT!!! I had one of these. A yellow 1990 GSI. It was a "performance" model. It was not all that fast (1.9L dual cam w/5spd)and could not corner very well. My stock Saturn SL1 corners better than my Storm did. <BR>If you want a good sports car, I would suggest another Fiero. Once you get rid of your Fiero, you will miss it! I had an 86 SE V-6 4spd drove it for 163,000 miles and got rid of it because it needed work and I didn't have time or money to deal with it. I had 3 more cars after it. Then I sat in a friends Fiero and within a month I had an 86 SE again! There is nothing else that compares to a Fiero. Even if the other car is faster or handles better you will always compare it to the Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||frontal lobe||04-16-2000||12:26 AM||||Cooter, I wasn't flaming you, buddy.  A Honda Civic is an excellent OTHER car.  Just not a substitute for a fiero.<P>Oreif, I was just joking about the Geo Storm.  Sporty cars should have engines bigger than motorcycles (or in the Storm's case, mopeds).<P>Spyder, NO WAY!! A new Vehicross, AND a 300zx in the stable???  Way to go!<P>Loafer87gt.  Saw a '91 mr2 turbo red 5-speed with leather interior 43000 miles for $7900US (don't know what that translates to in Canadian) in the paper today.  Milwaukee Journal-Sentinel.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Cooter||04-16-2000||12:45 AM||||I knew you were kidding, so no offense was taken. Besides, you have got to have something like a hatchback to haul your Fiero parts around in!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000018||Oreif||04-16-2000||01:08 AM||||Frontal, a moped engine!?! no wonder my Geo storm was slow! (LOL)<P>Loafer, what about the new Opal Speedster? I've heard rumors that Pontiac may build a clone for the states.<BR>||||reg||1
